{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "NMR", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Discovery: isolated from human amniotic fluid (2012 ref) as well as human broncho-alveolar-lavage (BAL) fluid (2020 ref). Sequence analysis: APD calcualted: molecular formula: C528H805N135O158S3; mol. wt: 11701.176; molar extinction coefficient: 20165; GRAVY= -0.74; Wimley-White whole-residue hydrophobicity of the peptide, 25.07 kcal/mol. Activity: Active against S. aureus ATCC25923, L. monocytogenes ATCC19115, S. epidermidis KCTC1917, E. coli ATCC25922, P. vulgaris KCTC2433 (MIC 0.3-2.4 uM). Antimicrobial conditions: it is more active against L. monocytogenes at acidic conditions pH 5.5 and below, characteristic of infection and inflammation. No activity at pH 6 or above ( Holch et al., 2020). Molecular form: It is in its non-aggregated form at pH 7 and shows fibril formation at pH 4.5 (Amyloid AMPs?). Structure: You can rotate, zoom, and view the crystal structure 1B1I here in the PDB. Updated 2/2014; 3/2023.", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "23144825", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "PLoS One. 2012;7(11):e47642. doi: 10.1371/journal.pone.0047642. PubMed; Gene Bank.", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP02343", "source_id": "AP02343", "source_numeric_id": "02343", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP02343", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Novel antibacterial activity of beta(2)-microglobulin in human amniotic fluid.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
